(FLW-26: a period ends the Repeat body and closes the construct; the
 statement after it belongs to the surrounding scope, so it runs ONCE
 (LANGUAGE.md:2294-2303). This is the regression guard for compiler bug
 #27 ("a period never closes a Repeat body"), fixed in v0.4.6 - before the
 fix this printed `r after r after`.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FLW-26.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   r
   r
   after
)
Repeat 2 times, print "r".
Print "after".
